1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,925
Most new traders put their stop in the wrong place.

2
00:00:03,294 --> 00:00:04,550
Or don't use one at all.

3
00:00:05,350 --> 00:00:09,006
Put it too tight, and ordinary noise stops you out of a good trade.

4
00:00:09,354 --> 00:00:13,770
Put it too wide, or skip it, and one bad trade can wipe out weeks of gains.

5
00:00:14,850 --> 00:00:21,033
A common rule is to place it just beyond the level that proves your idea wrong, like below the last swing low.

6
00:00:21,441 --> 00:00:27,672
Meme Street has chart tests on exactly this, and stop-losses you can practise with, using practice money.

7
00:00:28,172 --> 00:00:30,960
Practise placing your stops at memestreet.net.

